Widget.qml and Avatar.qml are derived from that project. The visual design, the
avatar rendering (shapes, colour handling, eyes, expressions, entrance and
gesture flourishes) and the bar/panel layout are theirs; the data layer here is
new, reading Rakazo's HTTP API instead of Grok Bot's local state directory, and
the settings, tests, setup tool and documentation have been rewritten for Rakazo.

Modified files
--------------
Widget.qml, Avatar.qml, and the avatar-cache helpers in bin/rakabot-watch are
changed versions of files from that project. Section 4(b) of the licence asks for
a prominent notice of modification, so each of those files carries a comment at
the top naming the original, the licence, and what changed. In short: the roster
is read from Rakazo's RPC API instead of Grok Bot's local state directory, the
palette and shape list are Rakazo's, the settings labels, status wording,
app-opening action, footer hint and demo roster are Rakazo's, and the panel's key
hint is measured rather than fixed.

New files, not derived from that project: bin/rakabot-setup, bin/rakabot-open,
scripts/, tests/, manifest.json, README.md, CHANGELOG.md, docs/ and this NOTICE.

